<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rayy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rayy was an ancient city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>, and a major centre on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> it was one of the cities, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nishapur">Nishapur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, from which sultans drew substantial revenue by taxing caravan traffic. It was devastated during the Mongol invasions of the thirteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rayy.jpg" alt="Rayy" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mohammad Hassanzadeh · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tughrul_Tower_-_6_January_2013_04_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
